{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e6ba0f6f7044b066fe23d5ec","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-n98pir"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"An annotation edit accepts text copied from a strings_compacted read, so a read-modify-write round trip silently truncates the stored entry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-11 on PR 1708 (a Greptile finding). To correct one timestamp, I read the newest pm-7zs0 comment with 'pm comments pm-7zs0 --json', replaced one word and wrote it back with 'pm comments pm-7zs0 --edit 270 --file <text>'. The default 3,000-token output budget had compacted that 900-character comment to a prefix ending in '…'. read_output reported strings_compacted: true and the page said truncated: true, but nothing stopped the edit, so the stored comment lost its second half. The same round trip is natural for notes and learnings, and for any agent that fixes a word in place. Duplicate check: searched output budget, compaction, truncation and annotation edit; pm-8eclqf, pm-gh1552 and pm-gh1478 (closed) bound and preserve reads, but none guards the write side of a compacted read."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","annotations","data-integrity","output-budget"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"An annotation --edit whose replacement text equals a compacted projection of the stored entry (a prefix ending in the compaction marker) is refused with a typed code naming the --output-budget unbounded or --limit read that returns the full text; Compacted strings in budgeted reads carry a marker the write path can recognise; Edits of genuinely new text ending in an ellipsis still succeed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A read-modify-write edit of an annotation never stores a budget-compacted prefix"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm comments --edit stored the compacted prefix of a 900-character comment without warning"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-8eclqf","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1478","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1552","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:05:52.810Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"98e4a3cf883cad03a63ca1b914cc6fe139341e84ce29fbd036974204255c7c16","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"