{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-12T21:55:16.403Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6cac702086723f6d9ab0b467","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1710","claim:pm-n98pir","lineage:pm-n98pir","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1710+pm-n98pir","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1710","claim:pm-n98pir","lineage:pm-n98pir","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-12T21:55:16.403Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-12T21:55:16.402Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation (2026-11-12). Compacted strings now carry a recognisable marker: compactExplanatoryString in src/core/shared/text-normalization.ts keeps the Unicode-safe 240-code-unit prefix and appends the ellipsis plus [+N chars], where N is the omitted UTF-16 code-unit count. Both compaction walkers use it, so JSON, TOON and the context-intent path agree. readCompactionMarker recognises only a trailing marker with a positive count (tolerating trailing whitespace), so a bare ellipsis or a marker quoted mid-text is ordinary text. runAnnotationCommand in src/sdk/annotations.ts refuses an --edit whose parsed replacement ends with the marker, before taking the item lock: annotation_text_compacted, exit 2, nothing written, with details collection, entry_index and omitted_characters, and examples naming the --output-budget unbounded read and the --file edit. The guard covers comments, notes and learnings (one shared path, so CLI, SDK and MCP alike). Appends are not refused, because quoting a compacted read as evidence is legitimate. Contract change: compacted strings used to end with a bare ellipsis."}]}],"before_hash":"8ec610d37035186adfdcc70f201d6193eb9f4f6628da43473f38df6a6eae5976","after_hash":"febd18de5c3981215075761fb92b69c46e3af0d639434f551307b9857909d9ea","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"03f08a3c3213d293aebfafd650a52e3f341e04403ec24b58838f7b9881a2df2f"}
